Hydrogel/TPU screen protector films for phones are typically classified as plastic articles. Candidates are 3926.90.99 (other articles of plastics) or 3919.90 (self-adhesive plates, sheets, film of plastics). Screen protectors are self-adhesive film, but they are cut to shape for a specific use. CBP rulings often place cell phone screen protectors in 3926.90.99 (for example, those made of TPU). Some rulings classify them in 3919.90.50 or 3919.90.60. Others consider them as accessories for phones in 8517.70, but that applies to parts, and screen protectors are not parts.

The most common classification is 3926.90.9990 for the "other" article of plastics; 3926.90.99 is the statistical suffix, "Other". The current HTS has 3926.90.9990 for other articles of plastics (since the 2022 revisions 3926.90.99.90 remains). I'll use that.

